  "coverage_summary": [
    "19 enabled time64 operations exercised through positive behavior across armel, armhf and native ARM64 controls; configured-off AIO is checked separately as ENOSYS.",
    "2100-01-01 timestamps round-trip through utimensat/statx and timerfd/POSIX timers.",
    "Only inside the guarded VM: clock_settime moves time to 2100, clock_gettime/208-byte clock_adjtime modes=0 observe it and original clock is restored. timex fraction validation follows STA_NANO.",
    "Legacy ARM32 clock/getres 8-byte and timerfd 16-byte layouts retain canaries; new timespec/itimerspec 16/32-byte layouts retain canaries.",
    "pselect sigarg and fdset placed at guard-page boundary; high pending RT63 remains masked across pselect/ppoll; original mask restored.",
    "recvmmsg validates two messages, nested iov, mmsghdr sizes and SCM_RIGHTS control data and closes the received descriptor.",
    "rt_sigtimedwait consumes an actually pending SIGUSR1 and validates architecture-specific siginfo sender-pid offset.",
    "Actual glibc2.44 ARM32 time64 wrappers accept beyond-INT32 timer values and 2100 clock values, with explicit matching isolated loaders.",
    "Signal-interrupted clock_nanosleep and raw pselect/ppoll validate 64-bit remaining-time copyback and canaries.",
    "Futex with beyond-INT32 relative timeout survives SIGSTOP/SIGCONT restart and wakes by the child shared-memory futex wake.",
    "Malformed times, pointers and sigset sizes return expected errors; compat-only dirty nsec high bits are masked, native64 rejects them."
  ],
